Many volumes have dependencies on a binary being on the node, such as ISCSI, RBD, Gluster, and even GitRepo.   If the binary is not present, CanSupport returns False and gives the user a "No plugins found" error.

A user has a reasonable expectation for, say, RBD to be supported and it requires debugging to understand the binary isn't present.  A better error message would be something like "RBD binary not installed".  CanSupport should return (bool, error) to support that.

