Kubernetes should add Cluster Scoped Resources .  Cluster Scoped resources are consumable resources that do not belong to any specific node but instead belong to the cluster.  A simple example are software licenses that can be shared through an network license server.  These resources should be tracked as normal consumable resources and should be usable by the scheduler when determining if a pod can actually be scheduled.

