It's bad when clients take a RV from one collection (e.g. pods) and list/watch on another collection (e.g., services). It's already caused some bugs with the cacher, and if we shard storage by collection it could be a bigger disaster. Therefore, we should take steps now to get clients out of the habit of doing this.

My idea is to just add some string, maybe just a letter or two, different by collection, and if we get a string that doesn't match we can reject the request or ignore the RV.

