@kubernetes/goog-control-plane did we change list/watch semantics recently?

For top-level API types that have a `Status` field, we usually create a subresource path for it on the API server, and make an `UpdateStatus()` method in the client library. The `Service.Status` is the only exception, it doesn't have either of them. Is there a particular reason to break this convention?

I raised the issue because in #19349 we are autogenerating the UpdateStatus() method for the client library. The generator generates the `UpdateStatus()` method for the [client for Service](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/19349/files#diff-6e7ec0db5816c399b12106abaad01f8bR80), but because there is no subresource path registered at the apiserver, that function will always fail.

