The test case "executing a command with run and attach without stdin" is inherently racy.

The test runs`kubectl run run-test --image=docker.io/library/busybox:1.29 --restart=OnFailure --attach=true --stdin -- sh -c cat && echo 'stdin closed'`, and expected to see `stdin closed` in the output.

The case when the test passes:
* case 1:
  * Kubernetes creates and starts the container without stdin;
  * The container exits before attach runs;
  * kubectl falls back to get container log, which contains `stdin closed`. https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/kubectl/cmd/run/run.go#L527
* case 2:
  * Kubernetes creates and starts the container without stdin;
  * kubectl attach before "stdin closed" is printed;
  * kubectl attach contains `stdin closed`.

The case when the test fails:
  * Kubernetes creates and starts the container without stdin;
  * The container prints "stdin closed", but hasn't exited yet;
  * kubectl attach contains nothing.

One example failure: https://gubernator.k8s.io/build/kubernetes-jenkins/logs/ci-containerd-e2e-ubuntu-gce/7057

Related issue: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/24070

Can we modify this test not to check the output? Or use `kubectl log` to check output instead?

