Verbose version of what was expected vs. how to reproduce:
ResourceAttributes documentation is inconsistent with experiments for SelfSubjectAccessReview.

Documentation says that '"*" means all' for 'verb' and 'group' (and other fields). This implies AND behavior, but it seems like it may instead be treated as an OR which should be described as 'any' (which is problematic when an AND check is desired).

Source:
https://github.com/kubernetes/api/blob/master/authorization/v1/types.go#L94,L97
Generated API reference:
https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/generated/kubernetes-api/v1.12/#resourceattributes-v1-authorization-k8s-io
(unchanged up through v1.15; test cluster had v1.12)

SelfSubjectAccessReview (`kubectl auth can-i`) was too permissive when "*" was used.

For a user that can only read and not write rolebindings, a specific check for "create" and "rolebindings" returned the expected result (no):

```
$ kubectl auth can-i get rolebindings
yes
$ kubectl auth can-i create rolebindings
no - no RBAC policy matched
Required "container.roleBindings.create" permission.
```

However, using `*` in place of the `create` verb yielded the unexpected "yes" (I expected `*` to be the AND of all can-i's for every verb). Similarly, using `*` in place of the rolebindings resource yielded the unexpected "yes" (I expected `*` to be the AND of all can-i's for `create` on every resource).

```
$ kubectl auth can-i "*" rolebindings
yes
$ kubectl auth can-i create '*'
yes
```

The same too-permissive behavior can be seen if "*" replaces either the verb or the API group in a manual curl SelfSubjectAccessReview. Request body was found with `kubectl auth can-i create rolebindings -v=500 2>&1 | grep "Request "`.

