@kelseyhightower

There are currently two different ways of determining request information: https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/apiserver/handlers.go#L264 and the system of record: https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/apiserver/api_installer.go#L97 that actually dispatches the calls.

Having two mechanisms for determining what verb/namespace/resource/subresource/etc information on the request means that the authorizer can end up out of sync with reality.  Collapsing the determination of request information to a single spot with a separate authorize call is one way to eliminate the duplication and avoid false authorization matches due to out of sync request information parsing.

