@davidopp @roberthbailey 

During talks with a potential client we've noticed a pretty common scenario that we do not support properly. If a client has some services outside of GCE (e.g. in a private datacenter) and some running on k8s cluster he'd want to have all of them discoverable. This can be achieved using VPN. The problematic part is that k8s cluster (on GCE and GKE) chooses a random subnet of 10.0.0.0 to be used for pods/services. That makes it pretty hard to preconfigure VPN and make sure there are no conflicts between GCE and private/other datacenter.

A simple solution would be to allow a user to specify a subnetwork that k8s cluster should use. From a brief discussion with @roberthbailey this should pretty easy to do using current APIs.

