I do not know whether you noticed already, but docker changed default format and location for the dockercfg. 
Previously it was `$HOME/.dockercfg` right now it's  `$HOME/.docker/config.json` and they slightly changed format:
#### previously

```
{
        "registryaddress": {
                "auth": "auth string",
                "email": "email@domain.com"
        }
}
```
#### current format

```
{
        "auths": {
                "registryaddress": {
                        "auth": "auth string",
                        "email": "email@domain.com"
                }
        }
}
```

and kubernetes requires to have "https://" prefix in order to work for old format, while docker doesn't require it, as a result, documentation at [http://kubernetes.io/v1.0/docs/](http://kubernetes.io/v1.0/docs/user-guide/images.html#configuring-nodes-to-authenticate-to-a-private-repository) it outdated and that's why you have so much "private registry" issues opened. 
So we either need to update documentation or to support new format, I personally think new format support is preferable, but it's up to you.

