Motivated by http://stackoverflow.com/questions/33606773/use-rbd-in-kubernetes-error

Currently Kubelet just logs "no volume plugins matched". 

What the plugin matching code does is:

```
    for k, v := range pm.plugins {
        if v.CanSupport(spec) {
            matches = append(matches, k)
        }
    }
```

The rbd CanSupport implementation checks whether the rbd command works:

```
func (plugin *rbdPlugin) CanSupport(spec *volume.Spec) bool {
    if (spec.Volume != nil && spec.Volume.RBD == nil) || (spec.PersistentVolume != nil && spec.PersistentVolume.Spec.RBD == nil) {
        return false
    }
    // see if rbd is there
    _, err := plugin.execCommand("rbd", []string{"-h"})
    if err == nil {
        return true
    }

    return false
}
```

If it doesn't, it's probably because the user didn't realize they needed to install it (the doc/example could be clearer).

However, CanSupport can't currently return an error string. The volume plugin interface should be changed to enable that, so that a useful error message could be returned.

