Previous issues for this test: #27394 #27660

`federation-controller-manager` runs within kubernetes inside a container.  It [needs access to CA certificates to work](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/27684).  At the moment, we are grabbing those certs [from the node filesystem](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/27802).

Do we wish to package this some other way?  If so, do we have a standard way of doing this?  Depending on what we choose, we may be on the hook for keeping this package up to date in the case that there's a security update.

