Persisting important config options in a salted file works, but we expose ourselves to bugs on every cluster update. I'm more confident about a solution that persists important information through the apiserver. 

One way to achieve this is: service controller comes up, looks for config map, if not found - looks for gce.conf:nodeTags and persists to config map. This would also allow a reconciliation loop that doesn't depend on in memory state.

